Why Are GaN HEMT Epitaxial Wafers Important?

GaN HEMT epitaxial wafers contain engineered semiconductor layers grown on substrates such as silicon, silicon carbide and sapphire. These layers create the electronic properties required for high-electron-mobility transistors.

The quality of epitaxial growth influences electron mobility, breakdown performance, RF characteristics and device reliability. Consequently, wafer suppliers must maintain strict control over thickness, uniformity and defect density.

5G and RF Applications Are Supporting Demand

GaN-based HEMTs are increasingly relevant to high-frequency communication systems. Their power-handling capabilities and operating characteristics make them suitable for RF applications, including telecommunications infrastructure, radar and aerospace systems.

The continued development of 5G networks is supporting demand for advanced GaN semiconductor materials.

Power Electronics Is Creating Additional Opportunities

GaN-on-Si technology offers opportunities in power switching applications, where efficiency and manufacturing economics are important. Applications include power conversion, electric vehicle charging and other high-efficiency electronic systems.

GaN-on-SiC remains particularly relevant to demanding RF applications because silicon carbide offers strong thermal conductivity.

Wafer Diameter and Epitaxial Quality Are Important Trends

The report covers wafers up to and including 4 inches, 6-inch wafers and 8-inch-and-above platforms. Larger wafer formats can improve manufacturing economics, provided that epitaxial uniformity and downstream device yields remain consistent.

